<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frans Post</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1612–1680</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frans Post was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> painter from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haarlem">Haarlem</a>, the first European artist to paint landscapes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. He travelled to Dutch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-maurits-of-nassau-siegen">Johan Maurits of Nassau-Siegen</a> and worked there from 1637 to 1644. After returning to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> he continued for decades to paint Brazilian scenes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> mills, plantations and river valleys from his sketches.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frans-post.jpg" alt="Frans Post" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Hals · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frans_Hals_-_Frans_Post_(Worcester_Art_Museum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
